      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f68684f2791d653bb4c0893|full_name} I'm with you. Names with special characters that can't be found by a standard keyboard stroke are also an issue. When you see names like this \"×͜x༒__×͜x༒\" you know it's created as to make it hard to ban them. That's just an example and that person hasn't done anything to me. I just simply hit x and that was the first to come up. \n\nHere are more examples:\n\nX△○▽X\n\nX×MΣᄂΛƬӨПIП×X\n\n×͜× x ×͜×\n\nX ۝ X\n\nThese special symbols can be so hard to replicate.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
